Immediate retries can extend caller waiting and worsen a persistent outage. Randomize backoff and consider shared retry accounting beyond per-call limits.

Book basis: [B4](/lore/durability-bibliography#b4-release-it), [B9](/lore/durability-bibliography#b9-serverless-architectures-on-aws), [B10](/lore/durability-bibliography#b10-a-philosophy-of-software-design), [B12](/lore/durability-bibliography#b12-site-reliability-engineering).

## Failure it prevents

Bounded requests collectively flood a recovering dependency, or nested retries multiply attempts.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`Effect.retry` and `Schedule.exponential`, `Schedule.jittered`, `Schedule.recurs`, and `Schedule.upTo` provide local policies. Shared budgets require an explicit owner and accounting [scope](/lore/scopes-own-resources).

Source: `packages/effect/src/Effect.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Schedule.ts`.

## How to check

Count attempts across the call path during a common outage. Check the declared total budget and caller deadline. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Circuit breakers have state](/lore/circuit-breakers-have-state), [Admission control protects recovery](/lore/admission-controls-new-work).

